@extends('layouts.public')@section('content')<article class="doc"><span class="eyebrow">THE MAILORA FIELD GUIDE</span><h1>A clear path from idea to inbox.</h1><h2>1. Set up your workspace</h2><p>Sign in, select a branch, and review Settings → Workspace. Enable the modules you need in Settings → Modules.</p><h2>2. Build a consented audience</h2><p>Create contacts with consent evidence, or publish a signup form. A pending contact cannot receive a campaign until confirmed.</p><h2>3. Create and approve your campaign</h2><p>Choose an audience, a verified sender, and a template. Include the unsubscribe merge tag. Save, approve, then queue the campaign.</p><h2>4. Run the worker</h2><pre>php artisan queue:work --tries=5
php artisan schedule:work</pre><p>Sandbox sends are stored in message logs. Paused campaigns can be resumed from the table action.</p><h2>API quick start</h2><p>Use a Sanctum bearer token with the contacts:read, contacts:write, or events:write ability. API routes also check module settings and role permissions.</p><pre>GET /api/v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN
Accept: application/json</pre><h2>Release scope</h2><p>The current implementation supports core audience, campaign, sandbox delivery, simple automation, signup forms, product/order records, deals, and tasks. Live SMTP delivery is available after HTTPS, SMTP credentials, and domain verification are configured. Billing gateways, advanced automation, and other catalog capabilities still require implementation. See docs/STATUS.md for the acceptance checklist.</p></article>@endsection